# Batch files are read by cmd.exe on Windows and want CRLF. An LF-only .bat
# can be mis-parsed inside a parenthesised block, which is exactly what
# "Start Roy R. Fisher.bat" contains, so this is correctness rather than
# tidiness. Marked here so git stores one form and checks out the other, and
# so `git diff --check` stops reporting the carriage returns as trailing
# whitespace.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# The packaged readme and the acceptance sheet are opened in Notepad.
*.txt text eol=crlf
